  "assumptions": [
    "Four independent lumped spin inertias; brush/sliding longitudinal law with regularized slip and a combined friction circle. Existing tire lateral relaxation and suspension contact remain.",
    "ABS/TCS are finite-rate pressure/torque modulation from slip, with ideal wheel-speed sensing. No universal stopping-distance improvement is asserted.",
    "Relative wheel spin acceleration reacts on the chassis. Steering-axis gyroscopic cross terms, full driveline dynamics, tire carcass thermodynamics and multi-body suspension are outside scope.",
    "Wing area .38 m², Cd .75, downforce coefficient1.1, moving wing-origin[0,.325+.30u,-2.065]m, incidence-.25u rad, a point.05m forward on the wing and1.5/s travel rate are engineering assumptions, not Tesla calibration.",
    "Delay/noise acts on flight position, velocity, attitude and angular-rate feedback. Wind is analytic; no CFD."
  ],
